&lt;div style=&quot;margin: 0px;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a motivated, detail-oriented &lt;strong&gt;Workers’ Compensation Adjuster &lt;/strong&gt;to joint our home health care organization.&amp;nbsp; This role will work closely with injured employees, office leadership, and our Third-Party Administrator (TPA) to support the day-to day-management of Workers’ Compensation claims while helping ensure injured employees receive timely care and support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an excellent opportunity for someone early in their Workers’ Compensation or claims career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;margin: 0px;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;: Under moderate supervision, will perform a variety of functions related to the management of the company’s Workers’ Compensation claims and other aspects of the Employee Claims and Safety office (ECS) through: 1) hands on management and creation of policies and practices, 2) preparing reports, analysis, and presentations, and 3) providing administrative and project support to your supervisor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Four (4) year college degree preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum two (2) years of experience in Workers’ Compensation claims handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic proficiency in handling litigated Workers’ Compensation claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in effectively and timely communicating with service offices, injured employees, and Third-Party Administrator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated record of strong interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven record of goal achievement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to handle multiple tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to arrange information and files in a useful manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft computer products including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Outlook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acceptable pre-employment assessment results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, write and effectively communicate in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn various aspects of the organization through technology training, hands-on learning, cross-training, and site visits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accurate completion of clerical functions such as the routine maintenance of reliable claim notes, records, and reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the company’s policies as well as the applicable state Workers’ Compensation laws that govern our work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted advisor and become a subject matter expert with regard to Employee Claims functions and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the team (office and company) and provide backup as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide customer service for routine claim questions, and direct more complex issues to BAYADA’s third party administrator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle a caseload between seventy-five (75) and one hundred fifty (150) active Workers’ Compensation claims while maintaining accurate and complete information on each assigned file.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No greater than 5% of caseload will be valued at greater than BAYADA’s current deductible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in infectious disease claims and communicating and implementing the associated BAYADA policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that each BAYADA office has a reliable Panel List of Providers and maintain regular contact with office directors to guarantee continued satisfaction with ECS’s outside medical vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that each work-related injury is reported within the state’s filing deadline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Obtain timely medical reports from claimant’s treating physicians and promptly inform BAYADA office staff of the findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule follow-up appointments for any claimant who misses a regularly scheduled medical visit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate placement of injured workers in modified or light-duty placements as directed by their treating physician; seek alternate work assignments for claimants if job opportunities do not exist within the company; facilitate completion of the company’s light-duty payroll on a weekly basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timely investigation of claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appropriate and accurate coding of claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continue to develop knowledge base of claims handling and jurisdictional knowledge through claims handling and independent research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timely completion of Action List items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to accurately evaluate and present settlement evaluations/recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to progressively work in a more independent fashion with moderate direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively works and collaborates with Third Party Administrator (TPA) and defense counsel to create effective strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing analysis of exposure and recommendations for mitigating the exposure and resolution of the claim is evidenced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identification of and escalation of Third-Party Administrator service issues through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously evaluate defense counsel and other strategic partnerships to ensure effectiveness and address issues as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the creation and management of policies, practices and procedures related to BAYADA’s Employee Claims and Safety office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate and independently research claim information through compilation of statistics, analyzing data and summarizing findings for review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in special projects: prepare reports and presentations using Microsoft Office (Word, PowerPoint etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BAYADA believes that our employees are our greatest asset:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Pay: $27-29 / hour plus bonus potential&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;depending on qualifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BAYADA offers a comprehensive benefits plan that includes the following: Paid holidays, vacation and sick leave, vision, dental and medical health plans, employer paid life insurance, 401k with company match, direct deposit and employee assistance program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To learn more about BAYADA Benefits, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bayada.com/benefits/&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
